# Build output
bin/
obj/
artifacts/

# IDE
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
# What Visual Studio writes when the browser head is opened with F5: a profile for an ASP.NET Core
# application, which this head is not, and one that makes F5 fail. It came back once already (3aa86b7).
src/AvCharts.Demo.Browser/Properties/launchSettings.json

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Test runs: hang dumps and sequence files (`--blame-hang-timeout`)
TestResults/

# Palette preview output: tools/palette-preview.py is the source of truth, the PNG is disposable
tools/palette-preview/

# Headless golden-image runs: `Received` is the diff output of a failing run, `Approved` is checked in
**/Golden/Received/

# Benchmark runs: the numbers belong in the design brief, the logs and reports are the run's own droppings
BenchmarkDotNet.Artifacts/

# The API documentation docfx generates from the built assemblies: it is read, not kept
docs/api/
